%% As built (R2-14): POST /events and the alert flow (api.py add_events; src/event_store.py)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Console
  participant A as api.py
  participant D as Detectors
  participant S as EventStore
  participant F as fusion.window_risks
  participant B as SQLite
  C->>A: POST /events {recipient, events[]}
  A->>D: _assess (same checks and scoring as /correlate; no time = server clock)
  A->>S: add(recipient, scored events)
  S->>S: HMAC-SHA256 of the recipient and each identity token
  S->>B: INSERT events (channel, time, score, label, model version, hashed tokens; text only if CP1_STORE_CONTENT=1)
  S->>B: SELECT the recipient's assessed events
  S->>F: window_risks(model, events, 60)
  F-->>S: each window with its risk (one window = one campaign)
  S->>B: UPSERT campaigns (key: recipient, first event); absorbed windows -> inactive
  opt a campaign reaches 0.5 for the first time
    S->>B: INSERT alert (events, shared tokens, reason); campaign.alerted = 1
  end
  S-->>A: event ids, new alerts
  A-->>C: campaigns, highest campaign risk, new alerts
  C->>A: GET /campaigns/{id}
  A-->>C: campaign + timeline (calls and video shown, not scored)
  C->>A: POST /alerts/{id}/ack
  A-->>C: acked
